73
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
He says: I took your advice to heart. this weekend

74
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Our pack goes on a camp out. every year.

75
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
I had about 10 weeblos on the camp out

76
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
and we selected a hike in the morning

77
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
and activity stations in the afternoon.

78
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Before we took the hike,

79
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
I told the boys to pick a leader for the weekend.

80
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
After they hashed it out amongst themselves,

81
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
I had a boy lead out for the hike.

82
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Things went pretty well,

83
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
although some of the boys didn't listen to their leader

84
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
quite as well as I would have hoped.

85
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Once or twice I had to reinforce the decision

86
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
the leader had made.

87
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
It was pretty awesome watching him talk to the boys,

88
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
get ideas and then choose an opinion

89
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
that both appealed to him

90
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
and the majority of the scouts.

91
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
In the afternoon

92
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
I had the leader divide the den into groups of five

93
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
and we went around and did the stations,

94
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
and after dinner I sat the boys down

95
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
and we talked about how they thought the day had gone

96
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
and what good reports and bad reports

97
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
I had gotten back what I thought had gone well,

98
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
and afterwards each boy got to talk about

99
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
the things he enjoyed most and the things he liked least.

100
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Overall, I think the boys had fun.

101
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
It gave them a good primer into what they'll be doing

102
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
in their scouting future and a scout troop.

103
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Thanks for all the great advice you give out.

104
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
That gave me the courage to break the mold

105
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
and let the boys have their first taste

106
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
of the patrol method.

107
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Thanks, Bryce, I'm happy to hear that.

108
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
It sounds like he handled it really well

109
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
with the Weeblos Den.

110
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
And just a slight caveat: a little bit of caution:

111
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
In a Weeblos Den the boys aren't ready

112
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
