115
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
But

116
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Bryce's example is a good example.

117
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
You know they can choose that leader

118
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
and the leader walks them around

119
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
and he has a lot of oversight

120
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
and input and reinforcement.

121
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
So we need to keep this kind of thing age-appropriate.

122
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
And then the reflection part

123
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
is the most important thing,

124
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
where we sit down at the end of the day

125
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
and we talk and the scouts talk

126
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
and everybody learns a little bit more

127
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
about why we're doing what we're doing.

